{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795683952,"nonce":"8u42566o4Vt3c4/dVcOcodEnzH8=","target":"df535ff651a62669a2f58cf294c26264bdd53fa6ab3575f98eff2408a761f753","message":"`ash --build` with three or more Rust static libraries as `--native-lib` fails in Apple's linker:\n\n    ld: Too many personality routines for compact unwind to encode. Found routines:\n      '_rust_eh_personality' (once per isolated object)\n\nReported by the hxn session on `--target aarch64-apple-ios-sim` with ash 0.1.22 and four libraries. Their window, GPU and 2D programs link three to five Rust libraries, so their iOS checks are blocked on this.\n\nCause: llvm/rust_isolate.rs merges each Rust archive, and the runtime, into one object and makes every symbol outside the interface local, including `rust_eh_personality`. Compact unwind encodes at most three personalities. The runtime counts as one, so the third library is one too many.\n\n`ASH_LINK_ARGS=-Wl,-no_compact_unwind` links, and must not be recommended: every Rust panic then aborts the process, \"fatal runtime error: failed to initiate panic, error 5, aborting\". It happens with two libraries and with four.\n\nCandidate fix, verified by hand outside the repository: on Mach-O targets add `_rust_eh_personality` to the exported symbol list of the `ld -r` merge, then set N_WEAK_DEF in that symbol's n_desc in the output object. The final link coalesces the copies. The references to follow are the CIE personality pointers in __TEXT,__eh_frame (pointer-to-GOT relocations that name the symbol), so one merged definition gives one personality.\n\nVerified with four Rust staticlibs linked into a C driver, each panicking inside its own catch_unwind, one through frames with destructors:\n\n- aarch64-apple-darwin: the current layout fails to link. The candidate links, every panic is caught and destructors run.\n- x86_64-apple-darwin (under Rosetta): the same.\n- aarch64-apple-ios-sim (spawned in a simulator): the same.\n\nNot verified: through `ash --build` itself, a device build for aarch64-apple-ios, and libraries built by different rustc versions. In that last case the linker keeps one copy of the personality for all of them. That copy reads the standard exception table, and each std still checks its own panics. This case is not tested. ELF targets have no such limit. Windows does not isolate libraries.\n\nTests wanted: in crates/ash_cli/tests/desktop_native_lib.rs, a program built from four Rust libraries on macOS that panics inside catch_unwind and returns the right result.","files":null}]}